>Complete Hand Drill Kit</td>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><b>Main Materials</b></span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Anodized Aluminum Alloy</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Tungsten Steel</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Aluminum Handle + Tungsten-Steel Bit Set</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><b>Bit Compatibility</b></span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">0.3–3.2 mm</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Bit diameters: 1 / 1.2 / 1.5 / 1.8 / 2 / 2.1 / 2.5 / 2.6 / 3 / 3.1 mm</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Same as individual components</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><b>Effective Bit Length</b></span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">—</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">8–12 mm</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">—</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><b>Clamping Method</b></span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Manual thread-tightened chuck</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Manual thread-tightened chuck</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Same as individual components</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><b>Special Design</b></span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Rear bearing for smoother rotation</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Color-coded rings + laser size marking</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Combination of both features</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><b>Recommended Use</b></span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Manual drilling, enlarging holes</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Precision hole adjustment on plastics, silicone, PCB</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">All-in-one solution for model drilling</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 18px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><b>Included Items</b></span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">1 × Handle</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">10 × Drill Bits</span></td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"width: 20%; height: 18px; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">1 Handle + 10 Drill Bits</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_padding-in-mobile\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\"><span style=\"font-size: 24px;\">Consideration</span></h2>\n<p></p>\n<p>To ensure safe and optimal performance:</p>\n<br/>\n<p><strong>When Using Small Bits (0.3 mm / 0.5 mm)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Use light pressure; excessive force may cause breakage</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Avoid drilling high-hardness materials with micro bits</span><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"></span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">General Safety &amp; Usage</span></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Always tighten the chuck manually before use to secure the bit</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Use safety goggles to protect against flying debris</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">For uneven surfaces, use a guide sleeve to prevent bit deflection</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">If a bit is dropped, inspect for cracks—replace if damaged</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">For high-accuracy drilling, pair with a dedicated model drilling stand</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
  "description_text": "Even with well‑calibrated printers, hole dimensions in FDM prints can vary slightly depending on material shrinkage, cooling, and layer orientation. This manual precision drill helps you carefully enlarge holes and refine tolerances without damaging delicate structures.\n\nSmall printed features or thin walls can crack easily when using powered drills. The manual drilling design provides direct tactile feedback, allowing you to gradually remove material and maintain precise control.\n\nThe anodized aluminum handle features a comfortable weighted grip, while the rear cap integrates a precision bearing. This allows the drill to rotate smoothly against your palm, improving stability and alignment when working with tiny holes.\n\nMade from high‑hardness tungsten steel, the bits maintain sharp edges for clean cuts in PLA, PETG, and ABS. Intuitive color‑coded rings and laser‑engraved markings make it easy to quickly find the exact size you need.\n\nThe hand drill handle is compatible with bits from 0.3 to 3.2 mm, and the included drill bit set covers commonly used sizes for 3D printing post-processing. It is ideal for clearing partially closed pilot holes, refining screw fits, and handling other precise manual drilling tasks.\n\nTo ensure safe and optimal performance:\n\nWhen Using Small Bits (0.3 mm / 0.5 mm)\n\nUse light pressure; excessive force may cause breakage\n\nAvoid drilling high-hardness materials with micro bits\n\nGeneral Safety & Usage\n\nAlways tighten the chuck manually before use to secure the bit\n\nUse safety goggles to protect against flying debris\n\nFor uneven surfaces, use a guide sleeve to prevent bit deflection\n\nIf a bit is dropped, inspect for cracks—replace if damaged\n\nFor high-accuracy drilling, pair with a dedicated model drilling stand",
